== 1. GW170817 alone: c_T^2 = 1/(1-beta) ==
  beta=+1e-15: c_T-1 = +4.44e-16
  beta=-1e-15: c_T-1 = -5.55e-16
  beta=+2e-15: c_T-1 = +8.88e-16
  beta=-6e-15: c_T-1 = -3.00e-15
  -> |beta| <~ 1e-15 (both signs bounded, GSS eq. 14)

== 2. beta = 0 section: maximal alpha allowed vs gamma ==
  bounds: weak-field (1e-4, 4e-7)
    gamma=1e-08: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 1.0e-08] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.00e+00
    gamma=1e-06: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 9.9e-07] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.00e+00
    gamma=1e-04: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 8.1e-07] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.11e+01
    gamma=1e-03: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 8.0e-07] (grid), c_S at amax = 3.53e+01
    gamma=1e-02: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 8.0e-07] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.11e+02
    gamma=5e-02: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 8.0e-07] (grid), c_S at amax = 2.41e+02
    gamma=1e-01: no allowed alpha on grid
  bounds: strong-field (1e-5, 1.6e-9)
    gamma=1e-08: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 1.0e-08] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.00e+00
    gamma=1e-06: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 3.2e-09] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.77e+01
    gamma=1e-04: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 3.2e-09] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.77e+02
    gamma=1e-03: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 3.2e-09] (grid), c_S at amax = 5.61e+02
    gamma=1e-02: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 3.2e-09] (grid), c_S at amax = 1.76e+03
    gamma=5e-02: allowed alpha in [1.0e-14, 3.2e-09] (grid), c_S at amax = 3.83e+03
    gamma=1e-01: no allowed alpha on grid

== 3. the two branches (beta = 0) ==
  alpha2 = (alpha/(2-alpha)) * (1 - alpha(1+2gamma)/gamma)
  branch (i): alpha << gamma -> alpha2 ~ alpha/2 -> alpha <~ 2|alpha2|max
  branch (ii): alpha ~ gamma/(1+2gamma) (cancellation) and alpha1 = -4alpha -> gamma ~ alpha <~ 2.5e-6;
               but then c_S^2 = (2-a)g/(a(2+3g)) ~ 1 -> borderline Cherenkov.
    gamma=1e-06, alpha=gamma/(1+2gamma)=1.000e-06: alpha1=-4.00e-06, alpha2=0.00e+00, c_S^2=1.0000, BBN=2.00e-06
    gamma=2e-06, alpha=gamma/(1+2gamma)=2.000e-06: alpha1=-8.00e-06, alpha2=0.00e+00, c_S^2=1.0000, BBN=4.00e-06

== 4. natural-prior volume (tuning measure) ==
  (alpha,gamma) uniform in [0,2]x[-0.3,1], beta=0, weak-field PPN, no Cherenkov: fraction allowed = 0/2000000 = 0.00e+00
  (beta adds a factor ~1e-15 of an O(1) interval)

== 5. strong-coupling scale at sample allowed points (M = reduced Planck) ==
  alpha=1e-06, gamma=0.01: allowed(weak)=False, allowed(strong)=False, c_S=9.93e+01, M_SC/M ~ 1.0e-04  (~2.4e+14 GeV)
  alpha=1e-09, gamma=0.01: allowed(weak)=True, allowed(strong)=True, c_S=3.14e+03, M_SC/M ~ 5.6e-07  (~1.4e+12 GeV)
  alpha=1e-09, gamma=0.1: allowed(weak)=False, allowed(strong)=False, c_S=9.33e+03, M_SC/M ~ 3.3e-07  (~7.9e+11 GeV)
  alpha=1e-12, gamma=0.01: allowed(weak)=True, allowed(strong)=True, c_S=9.93e+04, M_SC/M ~ 3.2e-09  (~7.6e+09 GeV)
  alpha=1e-15, gamma=0.01: allowed(weak)=True, allowed(strong)=True, c_S=3.14e+06, M_SC/M ~ 1.8e-11  (~4.3e+07 GeV)
  alpha -> 0 (Barausse/Franchini region alpha=beta=0): c_S -> inf, M_SC -> 0 (khronon strongly coupled).
